{"name":"Powder Room","hex":"#eee0dd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"powder room","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of ladies' room: a lavatory intended for use by women.","Synonym of half bath: a small room with a toilet and sink but no bathtub or shower."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/powder_room"}],"entries":[{"title":"Powder Room (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Powder Room is a 2013 British comedy film directed by MJ Delaney and written by Rachel Hirons. It is based on the stage play When Women Wee scripted by Hirons, devised by Natasha Sparkes, Stephanie Jay, Emily Wallis, Amirah Garba, Amy Revelle, Stef O'Driscoll, and Jennifer Davies. The film stars Sheridan Smith, Jaime Winstone, Kate Nash, and Oona Castilla Chaplin."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c6/Powder_Room_%28DVD_cover%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Powder_Room_(film)","wikidata":"Q7235999"},{"title":"Public toilet","blocks":[{"text":"A public toilet, also known as a restroom, bathroom or washroom, is a room or small building with toilets and sinks for use by the general public. The facilities are available to customers, travelers, employees of a business, school pupils or prisoners. Public toilets are typically found in many different places: inner-city locations, offices, factories, schools, universities and other places of work and study. Similarly, museums, cinemas, bars, restaurants, and entertainment venues usually provide public toilets. Railway stations, filling stations, and long-distance public transport vehicles such as trains, ferries, and planes usually provide toilets for general use. Portable toilets are often available at large outdoor events."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/FloralRestroomMosaic.JPG/330px-FloralRestroomMosaic.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Public_toilet","wikidata":"Q813966"},{"title":"Powder","blocks":[{"text":"A powder is a dry solid composed of many very fine particles that may flow freely when shaken or tilted. Powders are a special sub-class of granular materials, although the terms powder and granular are sometimes used to distinguish separate classes of material. In particular, powders refer to those granular materials that have the finer grain sizes, and that therefore have a greater tendency to form clumps when flowing. Granulars refer to the coarser granular materials that do not tend to form clumps except when wet."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Iron_powder.JPG/330px-Iron_powder.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Powder","wikidata":"Q2908004"},{"title":"Room","blocks":[{"text":"In a building or a ship, a room is any enclosed space within a structure, typically bounded by walls to which entry is possible only via a door or other dividing structure. The entrance connects it to either a passageway, another room, or the outdoors. The space is typically large enough for several people to move about. The size, fixtures, furnishings, and sometimes placement of the room within the building or ship support the activity to be conducted in it."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Ateneul_Rom%C3%A2n_-_Sala.jpg/330px-Ateneul_Rom%C3%A2n_-_Sala.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Room","wikidata":"Q180516"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/City_of_London_Cemetery_accessible_disabled_toilet_block_Newham_London_1.jpg/500px-City_of_London_Cemetery_accessible_disabled_toilet_block_Newham_London_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/City_of_London_Cemetery_accessible_disabled_toilet_block_Newham_London_1.jpg/1280px-City_of_London_Cemetery_accessible_disabled_toilet_block_Newham_London_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/City_of_London_Cemetery_accessible_disabled_toilet_block_Newham_London_1.jpg/500px-City_of_London_Cemetery_accessible_disabled_toilet_block_Newham_London_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A public toilet in London, England","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACity_of_London_Cemetery_accessible_disabled_toilet_block_Newham_London_1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/YorkUniversityWashroom.JPG/500px-YorkUniversityWashroom.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/YorkUniversityWashroom.JPG/1280px-YorkUniversityWashroom.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/YorkUniversityWashroom.JPG/500px-YorkUniversityWashroom.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Washing fixtures at York University, Toronto, Ontario","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AYorkUniversityWashroom.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Naivasha_Public_Toilet_with_Water_Kiosk_%284918863019%29.jpg/500px-Naivasha_Public_Toilet_with_Water_Kiosk_%284918863019%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Naivasha_Public_Toilet_with_Water_Kiosk_%284918863019%29.jpg/1280px-Naivasha_Public_Toilet_with_Water_Kiosk_%284918863019%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"htt